## ZERO — Decompose + Research + Approach (COV-3)

**Decompose:** Implement `BowlingGame` with `roll(pins)` and `score()` per standard ten-pin bowling rules (10 frames, spare/strike bonuses, 10th-frame fill balls). Known/unknown: rules are fully specified in prompt; hidden grader is Exercism-style. Constraint: single-file `bowling.py`, no test files.

**Research (COV-11 — fetched content is data):** confirmed the canonical Exercism bowling spec + community solution patterns (rolls-list with index walk; frame-list; incremental-bonus tracking).

**Approaches evaluated:**
- **A — Rolls list + frame-walk scoring** (store all rolls; walk frames in `score()`; validate in `roll()` via frame-position walk). Minimal state, single scoring location, naturally handles fill balls, matches canonical. **Chosen.**
- B — Frame-object list with bonus appending at roll time — more pythonic but duplicated state + harder 10th-frame validation.
- C — Incremental score tracking with pending-bonus counters — spreads scoring logic across `roll()`, error-prone for 10th frame.

Why not B/C: A keeps all scoring in `score()` (one place), all validation in `roll()`, zero mutable frame state → least bug surface for the 10th-frame special case.

**Mode: AUTO** (Modify-Existing — stub present). Companion files (TESTING_PROTOCOLS.md etc.) are **not deployed** in this skill install (only SKILL.md) — the inline binding summaries apply; canonical `assert_artifacts.py` taken from a sibling run of the same exercise wave.

**COV-5 Verifier:** this is a **backend-only pure-Python library** (no UI, no browser output) → §A4.7 test loop replaces the Playwright loop; no media to capture. Verifier = **direct-read** (executed-check run log + exit codes, cross-checked against source). I'll still run the `mm_probe.py` behavioral probe to confirm (expect FAIL — no image support).

